# 必考词 Unit05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit05核心高频词汇

{{concept}}{/ˈkɒnsept/}}{n. 概念；观念}}{{The concept of democracy has evolved over centuries.}}

{{conclude}}{/kənˈkluːd/}}{v. 得出结论；结束}}{{The study concluded that exercise improves mental health.}}

{{concrete}}{/ˈkɒŋkriːt/}}{adj. 具体的；n. 混凝土}}{{We need concrete evidence to support the argument.}}

{{condemn}}{/kənˈdem/}}{v. 谴责；判刑}}{{The international community condemned the terrorist attack.}}

{{conduct}}{/kənˈdʌkt/}}{v. 进行；指挥；n. 行为}}{{The scientist conducted a series of experiments in the lab.}}

{{conference}}{/ˈkɒnfərəns/}}{n. 会议；讨论会}}{{The annual conference attracted scholars from around the world.}}

{{confess}}{/kənˈfes/}}{v. 承认；坦白}}{{He confessed to making a serious error in judgment.}}

{{confidence}}{/ˈkɒnfɪdəns/}}{n. 信心；信任}}{{She spoke with great confidence during the presentation.}}

{{confine}}{/kənˈfaɪn/}}{v. 限制；禁闭}}{{The discussion was confined to the main topic.}}

{{confirm}}{/kənˈfɜːrm/}}{v. 确认；证实}}{{The experiment confirmed the hypothesis of the researchers.}}

{{conflict}}{/ˈkɒnflɪkt/}}{n. 冲突；矛盾}}{{The conflict between the two nations lasted for years.}}

{{confront}}{/kənˈfrʌnt/}}{v. 面对；对抗}}{{We must confront the challenges of climate change.}}

{{confuse}}{/kənˈfjuːz/}}{v. 使困惑；混淆}}{{The similar names often confuse the students.}}

{{congress}}{/ˈkɒŋɡres/}}{n. 国会；代表大会}}{{Congress passed a new bill on healthcare reform.}}

{{conscience}}{/ˈkɒnʃəns/}}{n. 良心；道德心}}{{His conscience prevented him from cheating on the exam.}}

{{conscious}}{/ˈkɒnʃəs/}}{adj. 有意识的；自觉的}}{{She was conscious of the need to save energy.}}

{{consensus}}{/kənˈsensəs/}}{n. 共识；一致}}{{The committee reached a consensus on the new policy.}}

{{consequence}}{/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/}}{n. 结果；后果}}{{Pollution is a consequence of industrial development.}}

{{conservative}}{/kənˈsɜːrvətɪv/}}{adj. 保守的；n. 保守派}}{{The party holds conservative views on social issues.}}

{{considerable}}{/kənˈsɪdərəbl/}}{adj. 相当大的；重要的}}{{The project requires a considerable amount of investment.}}

{{consist}}{/kənˈsɪst/}}{v. 由...组成；在于}}{{The team consists of ten experienced engineers.}}

{{consistent}}{/kənˈsɪstənt/}}{adj. 一致的；持续的}}{{Her performance has been consistent throughout the season.}}

{{constant}}{/ˈkɒnstənt/}}{adj. 不变的；持续的}}{{The machine operates at a constant temperature.}}

{{constitute}}{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt/}}{v. 构成；组成}}{{Women constitute more than half of the workforce.}}

{{construct}}{/kənˈstrʌkt/}}{v. 建造；构造}}{{The bridge was constructed in the 19th century.}}

{{consult}}{/kənˈsʌlt/}}{v. 咨询；查阅}}{{You should consult a doctor before taking any medication.}}

{{consume}}{/kənˈsjuːm/}}{v. 消耗；消费}}{{The new engine consumes less fuel than the old one.}}

{{contact}}{/ˈkɒntækt/}}{n./v. 接触；联系}}{{Please contact us if you have any questions.}}

{{contain}}{/kənˈteɪn/}}{v. 包含；控制}}{{The report contains valuable information about the market.}}

{{contemporary}}{/kənˈtempərəri/}}{adj. 当代的；n. 同时代的人}}{{Contemporary art often challenges traditional boundaries.}}

{{contempt}}{/kənˈtempt/}}{n. 轻视；蔑视}}{{He showed contempt for the rules and regulations.}}

{{contest}}{/ˈkɒntest/}}{n. 竞赛；v. 争辩}}{{She won first prize in the speech contest.}}

{{context}}{/ˈkɒntekst/}}{n. 上下文；背景}}{{The meaning of the word depends on the context.}}

{{contrast}}{/ˈkɒntrɑːst/}}{n./v. 对比；反差}}{{There is a sharp contrast between the two approaches.}}

{{contribute}}{/kənˈtrɪbjuːt/}}{v. 贡献；投稿}}{{Everyone should contribute to the protection of the environment.}}

{{controversial}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːrʃl/}}{adj. 有争议的}}{{The new policy has become a controversial topic of debate.}}

{{convention}}{/kənˈvenʃn/}}{n. 惯例；大会}}{{It is a social convention to shake hands when meeting someone.}}

{{convert}}{/kənˈvɜːrt/}}{v. 转变；转换}}{{The factory was converted into a modern art museum.}}

{{convince}}{/kənˈvɪns/}}{v. 使确信；说服}}{{He convinced the board to approve the investment plan.}}

{{cooperate}}{/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/}}{v. 合作；配合}}{{The two companies agreed to cooperate on the research project.}}
